-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Algorithms and constants followed

The Go implementation is this repository's own. To produce the same signals as
the reference implementations of the models it runs, it follows their
published pre- and post-processing parameters:

- YuNet decoding, score combination and NMS parameters, as in OpenCV's
  FaceDetectorYN (https://github.com/opencv/opencv, Apache License 2.0) and the
  opencv_zoo YuNet model (https://github.com/opencv/opencv_zoo, MIT).
- SFace input conventions and the reference thresholds returned by
  SFaceReferenceThresholds (cosine 0.363, L2 1.128), as published with
  OpenCV's FaceRecognizerSF and opencv_zoo (Apache License 2.0).
- BlazeFace short-range SSD anchor generation, decoding and weighted NMS
  parameters, as in Google MediaPipe's face detection graph
  (https://github.com/google-ai-edge/mediapipe, Apache License 2.0).
- The five-point 112x112 alignment template (ArcFaceTemplate), as published by
  the InsightFace project (https://github.com/deepinsight/insightface, code
  under the MIT License). Only the five coordinates are used; no InsightFace
  model or code is included.
- The least-squares similarity estimate of S. Umeyama, "Least-squares
  estimation of transformation parameters between two point patterns", IEEE
  TPAMI 13(4), 1991.
- MiVOLO input preprocessing, as described by the MiVOLO authors
  for iitolstykh/mivolo_v2 (Apache License 2.0).

